{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Y37QdzE1nyDdAfHF8MB8g","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"No, the dedicated configuration to cap maximum size of headers (initially `streams.store.headers.max.bytes`) was not kept in the final design of KIP-1271 (Allow to Store Record Headers in State Stores) as of January 2026.\\\\n\\\\nSupporting facts in time order:\\\\n- On 2026-01-12T21:07:50.000000Z, Alieh Saeedi stated that the maximum header length is a fixed 2-byte hard limit (64 KB) and that the configuration could be removed [mail:fddcc74d4df53f96c1a36885].\\\\n- On 2026-01-12T23:07:23.000000Z, Matthias J. Sax asked to remove the configuration from the KIP [mail:f02043314bea5e4bc5754aae].\\\\n- On 2026-01-14T18:39:56Z, Alieh Saeedi confirmed removal: \\\\\\\"I have removed the two-byte header size and its associated configuration property.\\\\\\\" [mail:1c0b316b9c6624add1f97d07]\\\\n- On 2026-01-16T17:00:39.000000Z, the design introduced a varint `header_size` field for lazy deserialization, with no mention of a cap configuration [mail:cc6691acddb4132e5b46a141].\\\\n\\\\nWhat could not be determined: The JIRA records for KAFKA-20056 contain no comments or changelog entries mentioning the configuration, and the Confluence KIP-1271 page is not included in the provided records; however, the mailing-list evidence directly confirms the removal.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"mail:fddcc74d4df53f96c1a36885\\\",\\\"mail:f02043314bea5e4bc5754aae\\\",\\\"mail:1c0b316b9c6624add1f97d07\\\",\\\"mail:cc6691acddb4132e5b46a141\\\",\\\"mail:56a76d3a2f1c08227d88d1f4\\\",\\\"mail:bd104003033b64b1b66392f7\\\",\\\"jira:13638629:change:22875142:0\\\",\\\"jira:13638629:change:22875263:0\\\",\\\"jira:13638629:change:22875264:0\\\",\\\"jira:13638629:change:22875265:0\\\",\\\"jira:13638629:change:22875266:0\\\",\\\"jira:13638629:change:22886433:0\\\",\\\"mail:0d16a5e0a2869739fe6f8982\\\",\\\"mail:a2edcbf70ee73837ad13fac1\\\",\\\"mail:a0a49e52c583570dfe5ca142\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":238.376,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":14,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0083967,\\\"input_tokens\\\":179027,\\\"output_tokens\\\":24059}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e06f8d4-86af-49a9-9aa8-f26924a18033","uuid":"be0588ac-a345-4b66-b33f-0fb878a4efb7","timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:44:43.631Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"No, the dedicated configuration to cap maximum size of headers (initially `streams.store.headers.max.bytes`) was not kept in the final design of KIP-1271 (Allow to Store Record Headers in State Stores) as of January 2026.\\\\n\\\\nSupporting facts in time order:\\\\n- On 2026-01-12T21:07:50.000000Z, Alieh Saeedi stated that the maximum header length is a fixed 2-byte hard limit (64 KB) and that the configuration could be removed [mail:fddcc74d4df53f96c1a36885].\\\\n- On 2026-01-12T23:07:23.000000Z, Matthias J. Sax asked to remove the configuration from the KIP [mail:f02043314bea5e4bc5754aae].\\\\n- On 2026-01-14T18:39:56Z, Alieh Saeedi confirmed removal: \\\\\\\"I have removed the two-byte header size and its associated configuration property.\\\\\\\" [mail:1c0b316b9c6624add1f97d07]\\\\n- On 2026-01-16T17:00:39.000000Z, the design introduced a varint `header_size` field for lazy deserialization, with no mention of a cap configuration [mail:cc6691acddb4132e5b46a141].\\\\n\\\\nWhat could not be determined: The JIRA records for KAFKA-20056 contain no comments or changelog entries mentioning the configuration, and the Confluence KIP-1271 page is not included in the provided records; however, the mailing-list evidence directly confirms the removal.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"mail:fddcc74d4df53f96c1a36885\\\",\\\"mail:f02043314bea5e4bc5754aae\\\",\\\"mail:1c0b316b9c6624add1f97d07\\\",\\\"mail:cc6691acddb4132e5b46a141\\\",\\\"mail:56a76d3a2f1c08227d88d1f4\